  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason—presence of a sure outcome—is explicitly recognized by the individual, who contrasts the sure outcome in A with the uncertain (though highly probable) outcomes in B. The individual’s justification ('sicher ist sicher') directly aligns with the rule of the decision reason, which prefers the lottery with a sure outcome. The mention of the 1% loss chance in B further confirms that the individual noticed the lack of certainty in B. Their rejection of the higher potential gain in B due to the lack of certainty reinforces that the presence of a sure outcome was central to their choice. Both the considered information and the justification match the decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 100
}

